//
// A NON-PUB METHOD IS REFUSED THROUGH THE QUALIFIER (`@FR-F-Surface`; found walking its pair with
// `@FR-Disp-Trigger`, whose triggers derive only from the pub surface).  `fn fs_tm(self: text)`
// is declared without `pub`, so `f_surface_fixture_lib::fs_tm("hi")` is an outside reach of a
// non-pub item and must be refused exactly as the non-pub plain function is.
//
// Guards loft#2115: the call was accepted and printed "hi." on both backends — a qualified call
// asked the library for the item by NAME, and a method is keyed by its receiver.  The method
// spelling on the library's own record is the cell beside this one.
//
// @falsified-at: e71f24b34 — accepted there (prints "hi."), interpret and native.
// CHANNEL: the compile (the expected diagnostic).
// ARMED: no instrument.
// WITNESS: the diagnostic names the item and the library.
// HOLDS: `a-non-pub-function-is-refused-through-the-qualifier` beside it.
// @EXPECT_ERROR: `fs_tm` is not `pub` in `f_surface_fixture_lib`

fn main() {
  println(f_surface_fixture_lib::fs_tm("hi"));
}
